    296  f0cc
    297  f0cc							; --- E4 moth body (bank2 free space $F008-$F9D8) -------------------------
    298  f0cc							; Entered from bank0 via the $FEF0 entry tramp (sta $1FF8 lands on the
    299  f0cc							; jmp below at $FEF3). Exits via `jmp MothExitPad` ($FC49): bank2 runs
    300  f0cc							; sta $1FF6, bank0 serves jmp UE_Next. Rules:
    301  f0cc							;   - NEVER jsr FoldIndirect or any bank0 routine (a fold from inside
    302  f0cc							;     bank2 would switch away mid-routine = frozen player).
    303  f0cc							;   - Enemy records ARE here (org $F9D9) — read directly, no fold needed.
    304  f0cc							;   - Keep the whole routine inline (no jsr): tramps are tail jmps so
    305  f0cc							;     the stack depth equals the UE body (+0 vs the $F8 guard).
    306  f0cc							;   - ZP (rect cache, EnemyRam*, EnemyDataLo/Hi) is RAM: bank-independent.
    307  f0cc		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$F110 - *, 0
    308  f110				   MothRoutine
    309  f110							; E4 Stage C: horizontal patrol (docs/e4_moth_plan.md). 1 px / 2 frames
    310  f110							; (EnemyRamP & 1), range = spawn ± 8 tiles (32 px), wall/range/wrap =
